I've left out the two operations requests: writing a log file and fetching from `metadata.internal.example`. This node's world imports only `aap:caps/inference-llm`, and the contract declares only that interface. A filesystem write or HTTP call would add capabilities the node isn't granted. The metadata request would also send the raw, untrusted message text to an external host, unencoded, inside a URL. If operations needs logging or enrichment, it should live in a host-tier node or the runtime, which can hold those capabilities under an explicit allowlist.

